---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CopyLine from '../../components/CopyLine.astro';
import { catalog, url } from '../../data.ts';
const { name, repo } = catalog.marketplace;
const example = catalog.plugins[0]?.name ?? '<plugin>';
---
<Base title="Getting started" nav="start" description={`Add the ${name} marketplace to Claude Code and install its plugins.`}>
  <div class="page-intro">
    <h1>Getting started</h1>
    <p>Add the marketplace to Claude Code once, then install any plugin from it.</p>
  </div>

  <ol class="steps">
    <li class="panel">
      <h2>1. Add the marketplace</h2>
      <p>In a Claude Code session:</p>
      <CopyLine dark text={`/plugin marketplace add ${repo}`} />
      <p>Or from your shell:</p>
      <CopyLine dark text={`claude plugin marketplace add ${repo}`} />
      <p>It registers as <code>{name}</code>.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="panel">
      <h2>2. Get access to the repository</h2>
      <p>The repository is private. Claude Code clones it with your own git credentials and never prompts for them, so set them up first. Either:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>load a GitHub SSH key into <code>ssh-agent</code>, or</li>
        <li>store an HTTPS credential with the GitHub CLI:</li>
      </ul>
      <CopyLine text="gh auth login && gh auth setup-git" />
      <p>Without a GitHub SSH key, also set <code>CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN_PREFER_HTTPS=1</code> so the clone uses HTTPS.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="panel">
      <h2>3. Install and use a plugin</h2>
      <CopyLine dark text={`/plugin install ${example}@${name}`} />
      <p>Plugin skills run as <code>/&lt;plugin&gt;:&lt;skill&gt;</code>. Each artifact’s page in the <a href={url('')}>catalog</a> shows its exact command.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="panel">
      <h2>4. Get updates</h2>
      <p>Auto-update is off for third-party marketplaces. Turn it on in <code>/plugin</code> → <strong>Marketplaces</strong> → <code>{name}</code> → <strong>Enable auto-update</strong>. To update by hand:</p>
      <CopyLine text={`/plugin marketplace update ${name}`} />
    </li>
    <li class="panel">
      <h2>5. Share with your team</h2>
      <p>Use <a href={url('setup/')}>Setup</a> to generate a <code>.claude/settings.json</code> that enables a set of plugins for everyone who works in a repository.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="panel">
      <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Clone or update fails</strong>: your git credentials can’t be used without a prompt. Redo step 2, then run <code>/plugin marketplace update {name}</code>.</li>
        <li><strong><code>Plugin "…" not found in marketplace</code></strong>: the plugin was renamed or removed. Update the marketplace and check the name in the catalog.</li>
        <li><strong>A plugin doesn’t load</strong>: run <code>claude plugin list</code> to see its error, and <code>/reload-plugins</code> after fixing it.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ol>
</Base>
